      "text": "LangGraph checkpoints are a persistence system that records a thread's graph state after each execution step, enabling short-term, thread-scoped memory for conversation continuity, human-in-the-loop workflows, time travel, and fault tolerance [doc-99e58642fe77::0000]."
    },
    {
      "type": "citations",
      "turn_id": "d80c44fb631b42d9938a5594d35caaf5",
      "sequence": 96,
      "timestamp": "2026-10-26T18:20:26.745444+00:00",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "doc-99e58642fe77::0000",
          "score": 0.59010756,
          "text": "Persistence lets LangGraph applications keep useful information beyond a single graph run. It matters when an agent needs to continue a conversation, resume after an interruption, recover from a failure, or remember information across interactions.\nLangGraph provides two complementary persistence systems:\nCheckpointers\npersist a thread\u2019s graph state as checkpoints. Use them for short-term, thread-scoped memory, including conversation continuity, human-in-the-loop workflows, time travel, and fault tolerance.\nStores\npersist application-defined data outside the graph state. Use them for long-term, cross-thread memory, including user preferences, facts, and shared knowledge.\nMost applications can use both: a\ncheckpointer\ntracks the current thread, and a\nstore\ntracks durable information across threads.\n##  Quickstart\nCompile your graph with a checkpointer, a store, or both:",
          "chunk_order": 0.0,
          "content_hash": "12065604856b8437c1d1d1f8c006dc0d466c88a7bbbdafeb9ac034618b16310b",
          "corpus_version": "docs-v1",
          "document_id": "doc-99e58642fe77",
          "heading": "Quickstart",
          "kind": "chunk",
          "snapshot_date": "2026-10-26T07:59:59.902853+00:00",
          "title": "Persistence - Docs by LangChain",
          "topic": "langgraph",
          "url": "https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/persistence"
        }
      ]
    },
